thout MT. `POOL_*` degenerate to synchronous.\n\n### 1.14 dictBuilder\n`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` (= fastCover optimize, d=8, steps=4, level=3), `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover`, `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover`, `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover`, `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover`, `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy`, `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary`, `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer`, `ZDICT_getDictID`, `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize`, `ZDICT_isError`, `ZDICT_getErrorName`,\nCOVER internals: `COVER_best_init/start/wait/finish/destroy`, `COVER_selectDict`, `COVER_dictSelectionError/Free/IsError`, `COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize`, `COVER_computeEpochs`, `COVER_sum`, `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus`, `divsufsort`, `divbwt`\n\n### 1.15 Deprecated ZBUFF_*\n`ZBUFF_createCCtx`, `_advanced`, `ZBUFF_freeCCtx`, `ZBUFF_compressInit`, `_advanced`, `ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary`, `ZBUFF_compressContinue`, `ZBUFF_compressFlush`, `ZBUFF_compressEnd`, `ZBUFF_createDCtx`, `_advanced`, `ZBUFF_freeDCtx`, `ZBUFF_decompressInit`, `ZBUFF_decompressInitDictionary`, `ZBUFF_decompressContinue`, `ZBUFF_isError`, `ZBUFF_getErrorName`, `ZBUFF_recommendedCInSize/COutSize/DInSize/DOutSize`\n\n### 1.16 Legacy decoders (v01..v07)\n- v01: `ZSTDv01_decompress`, `_decompressDCtx`, `createDCtx`, `freeDCtx`, `resetDCtx`, `nextSrcSizeToDecompress`, `decompressContinue`, `isError`, `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` (magic `0xFD2FB51E`)\n- v02: `ZSTDv02_*` same shape (magic `0xFD2FB522`)\n- v03: `ZSTDv03_*` (magic `0xFD2FB523`)\n- v04: `ZSTDv04_*` + `ZBUFFv04_*` (magic `0xFD2FB524`)\n- v05: `ZSTDv05_*` incl. `decompressBegin(_usingDict)`, `decompressBlock`, `decompress_usingDict`, `decompress_usingPreparedDCtx`, `copyDCtx`, `getFrameParams`, `sizeofDCtx` + `ZBUFFv05_*` + `FSEv05_*`, `HUFv05_*` (magic `0xFD2FB525`)\n- v06: `ZSTDv06_*` + `ZBUFFv06_*` + `FSEv06_*`, `HUFv06_*` (magic `0xFD2FB526`)\n- v07: `ZSTDv07_*` incl. `createDDict`/`freeDDict`/`decompress_usingDDict`/`insertBlock`/`isSkipFrame`/`estimateDCtxSize` + `ZBUFFv07_*` + `FSEv07_*`, `HUFv07_*` (magic `0xFD2FB527`)\n- Automatic dispatch (`ZSTD_isLegacy`) recognizes **only 5, 6, 7** under `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5`; v01..v04 are reachable only by calling their symbols directly.\n\n### 1.17 Entropy / utility exports\n- FSE: `FSE_versionNumber`, `FSE_compressBound`, `FSE_isError`, `FSE_getErrorName`, `FSE_optimalTableLog`, `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal`, `FSE_normalizeCount`, `FSE_NCountWriteBound`, `FSE_writeNCount`, `FSE_readNCount`, `FSE_readNCount_bmi2`, `FSE_buildCTable_wksp`, `FSE_buildCTable_rle`, `FSE_compress_usingCTable`, `FSE_buildDTable_wksp`, `FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2`\n- HIST: `HIST_count`, `HIST_count_simple`, `HIST_count_wksp`, `HIST_countFast`, `HIST_countFast_wksp`, `HIST_add`, `HIST_isError`\n- HUF: `HUF_compressBound`, `HUF_optimalTableLog`, `HUF_minTableLog`, `HUF_cardinality`, `HUF_buildCTable_wksp`, `HUF_writeCTable_wksp`, `HUF_readCTable`, `HUF_readCTableHeader`, `HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable`, `HUF_validateCTable`, `HUF_estimateCompressedSize`, `HUF_compress1X_usingCTable`, `HUF_compress4X_usingCTable`, `HUF_compress1X_repeat`, `HUF_compress4X_repeat`, `HUF_readDTableX1_wksp`, `HUF_readDTableX2_wksp`, `HUF_decompress1X_DCtx_wksp`, `HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp`, `HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx_wksp`, `HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly_wksp`, `HUF_decompress1X_usingDTable`, `HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable`, `HUF_selectDecoder`, `HUF_readStats`, `HUF_readStats_wksp`, `HUF_isError`, `HUF_getErrorName`\n- XXH (namespaced): `ZSTD_XXH32`, `ZSTD_XXH32_createState/freeState/reset/update/digest/copyState/canonicalFromHash/hashFromCanonical`, same for `ZSTD_XXH64_*`, `ZSTD_XXH_versionNumber`\n- POOL: `POOL_create`, `POOL_create_advanced`, `POOL_free`, `POOL_resize`, `POOL_sizeof`, `POOL_add`, `POOL_tryAdd`, `POOL_joinJobs`\n- match-finder / internals exported: `ZSTD_compressBlock_{fast,doubleFast,greedy,lazy,lazy2,btlazy2,btopt,btultra,btultra2}` × `{plain,_row,_extDict,_extDict_row,_dictMatchState,_dictMatchState_row,_dedicatedDictSearch,_dedicatedDictSearch_row}`, `ZSTD_selectBlockCompressor`, `ZSTD_fillHashTable`, `ZSTD_fillDoubleHashTable`, `ZSTD_row_update`, `ZSTD_insertAndFindFirstIndex`, `ZSTD_updateTree`, `ZSTD_ldm_*` (9 symbols), `ZSTD_reset_compressedBlockState`, `g_debuglevel`, `g_ZSTD_threading_useless_symbol`\n\n---\n\n# SECTION 2 — Axes of variation with concrete values\n\n## 2.1 Compression level\n- `ZSTD_minCLevel() = -ZSTD_TARGETLENGTH_MAX = **-131072**`; `ZSTD_maxCLevel() = **22**`; `ZSTD_defaultCLevel() = ZSTD_CLEVEL_DEFAULT = **3**`.\n- `ZSTD_c_compressionLevel` is **clamped** (not rejected) to `[-131072, 22]`. Value `0` → 3.\n- Negative levels use table row 0 and set `targetLength = -clampedLevel` (an \"acceleration factor\").\n- Row selection: `tableID = (rSize<=256KB) + (rSize<=128KB) + (rSize<=16KB)` where `rSize` derives from srcSizeHint/pledgedSrcSize/dictSize → **4 distinct cParam tables**. Same level yields different strategies per table.\n\nLevel → strategy, **tableID 0** (srcSize unknown or >256 KB) — from `clevels.h`:\n\n| ZSTD_strategy | value | levels selecting it (tableID 0) | representative level |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ZSTD_fast | 1 | ≤0 (row 0), 1, 2 | **1** (and **-5**, **-131072**) |\n| ZSTD_dfast | 2 | 3, 4 | **3** |\n| ZSTD_greedy | 3 | 5 | **5** |\n| ZSTD_lazy | 4 | 6, 7 | **6** |\n| ZSTD_lazy2 | 5 | 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 | **9** |\n| ZSTD_btlazy2 | 6 | 13, 14, 15 | **13** |\n| ZSTD_btopt | 7 | 16, 17 | **16** |\n| ZSTD_btultra | 8 | 18 | **18** |\n| ZSTD_btultra2 | 9 | 19, 20, 21, 22 | **19** |\n\nTable-ID cross-check values worth exercising (same level, different table): level 2 → `fast` (tbl0/2/3) vs `dfast` (tbl1); level 4 → `dfast` (tbl0) / `greedy` (tbl1) / `dfast` (tbl2) / `greedy` (tbl3); level 11 → `lazy2` (tbl0) / `btlazy2` (tbl1,2) / `btopt` (tbl3). Drive with `ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint` = `0`, `10000` (≤16 KB), `100000` (≤128 KB), `200000` (≤256 KB), `1000000` (>256 KB).\n\n## 2.2 All `ZSTD_cParameter` accepted by `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter`\n\n| enum | value | bounds (this build) | 0 means | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_c_compressionLevel` | 100 | clamp `[-131072, 22]` | default 3 | selects whole cParam row; also feeds `ZSTD_resolveExternalRepcodeSearch` (cLevel<10 → disable) |\n| `ZSTD_c_windowLog` | 101 | `[10, 31]` | auto | max back-ref distance; >14 enables row-MF in auto; ≥17 enables post block splitter in auto (with strategy≥btopt); ≥27 enables LDM in auto |\n| `ZSTD_c_hashLog` | 102 | `[6, 30]` | auto | initial probe table size; `hashLog > chainLog` required for DDS |\n| `ZSTD_c_chainLog` | 103 | `[6, 30]` | auto | multi-probe table; not allocated for `fast` or row-MF; `≤24` required for DDS |\n| `ZSTD_c_searchLog` | 104 | `[1, 30]` | auto | nb search attempts |\n| `ZSTD_c_minMatch` | 105 | `[3, 7]` | auto | 3 only meaningful for btopt+; 7 only for fast; others clamped to 4..6 |\n| `ZSTD_c_targetLength` | 106 | `[0, 131072]` | 0 valid | opt-parser accept length; for `fast`/`dfast` it is the negative-level acceleration |\n| `ZSTD_c_strategy` | 107 | `[1, 9]` = `ZSTD_fast..ZSTD_btultra2` | auto | picks block compressor |\n| `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize` | 130 | `[1340, 131072]`, values 1..1339 silently raised to 1340 | disabled | enables superblock/`ZSTD_compressBlock_targetCBlockSize` path; **rejected by `ZSTD_generateSequences`** |\n| `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching` | 160 | `[0,2]` = auto/enable/disable | auto | when enabled, forces `windowLog = 27` unless overridden |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmHashLog` | 161 | `[6, 30]` | auto | LDM table size |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch` | 162 | `[4, 4096]` | default 64 | LDM min match |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmBucketSizeLog` | 163 | `[1, 8]` | default 3 | LDM bucket |\n| `ZSTD_c_ldmHashRateLog` | 164 | `[0, 25]` (`WINDOWLOG_MAX-HASHLOG_MIN`) | auto | LDM insertion rate |\n| `ZSTD_c_contentSizeFlag` | 200 | `[0,1]` (any nonzero→1) | off | writes FCS in frame header |\n| `ZSTD_c_checksumFlag` | 201 | `[0,1]` | off | appends 4-byte XXH64-low32 checksum |\n| `ZSTD_c_dictIDFlag` | 202 | `[0,1]` | sets `noDictIDFlag=!value` | writes dictID in header |\n| `ZSTD_c_nbWorkers` | 400 | `[0, 0]` | — | **non-zero → `parameter_unsupported`** |\n| `ZSTD_c_jobSize` | 401 | `[0, 0]` | — | **non-zero → `parameter_unsupported`**; `getParameter` also errors |\n| `ZSTD_c_overlapLog` | 402 | `[0, 0]` | — | **non-zero → `parameter_unsupported`** |\n| `ZSTD_c_rsyncable` (`experimentalParam1`) | 500 | `[0, 1]` per bounds, but setter rejects non-0 | — | **non-zero → `parameter_unsupported`** |\n| `ZSTD_c_format` (`experimentalParam2`) | 10 | `[0, 1]` = `ZSTD_f_zstd1`/`ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless` | zstd1 | omits 4-byte magic |\n| `ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow` (`experimentalParam3`) | 1000 | `[0, 1]` | off | forces max window in header; also **disables CDict attach** |\n| `ZSTD_c_forceAttachDict` (`experimentalParam4`) | 1001 | `[0, 3]` = DefaultAttach/ForceAttach/ForceCopy/ForceLoad | default | overrides `ZSTD_shouldAttachDict` heuristic |\n| `ZSTD_c_literalCompressionMode` (`experimentalParam5`) | 1002 | `[0, 2]` auto/enable/disable | auto (neg levels → uncompressed) | raw vs HUF literals |\n| *`experimentalParam6`* | 1003 | **removed** | — | `parameter_unsupported` (negative test) |\n| `ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint` (`experimentalParam7`) | 1004 | `[0, 2147483647]` | off | feeds cParam table-ID selection |\n| `ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch` (`experimentalParam8`) | 1005 | `[0, 1]` | off | DDS CDict; requires `greedy≤strategy≤lazy2 && hashLog>chainLog && chainLog≤24` |\n| `ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer` (`experimentalParam9`) | 1006 | `[0, 1]` buffered/stable | buffered | `input.src`+`pos` must be identical across calls else `stabilityCondition_notRespected` |\n| `ZSTD_c_stableOutBuffer` (`experimentalParam10`) | 1007 | `[0, 1]` | buffered | `output.size-output.pos` must be constant |\n| `ZSTD_c_blockDelimiters` (`experimentalParam11`) | 1008 | `[0, 1]` noBlockDelimiters/explicitBlockDelimiters | no delims | sequence-array interpretation; `compressSequencesAndLiterals` **requires explicit** |\n| `ZSTD_c_validateSequences` (`experimentalParam12`) | 1009 | `[0, 1]` | off | validate external seqs; `compressSequencesAndLiterals` **rejects 1** |\n| `ZSTD_c_splitAfterSequences` (`experimentalParam13`, a.k.a. `useBlockSplitter`) | 1010 | `[0, 2]` auto/enable/disable | auto = `strategy≥btopt && windowLog≥17` | post-block splitter |\n| `ZSTD_c_useRowMatchFinder` (`experimentalParam14`) | 1011 | `[0, 2]` | auto = supported(greedy..lazy2) && windowLog>14 | row hash MF; also changes chainTable allocation |\n| `ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix` (`experimentalParam15`) | 1012 | `[0, 1]` | off | forces prefix relocation for reproducibility |\n| `ZSTD_c_prefetchCDictTables` (`experimentalParam16`) | 1013 | `[0, 2]` | auto | prefetch attached-CDict tables (perf only, must not change output) |\n| `ZSTD_c_enableSeqProducerFallback` (`experimentalParam17`) | 1014 | `[0, 1]` | off | fallback when external seq producer fails |\n| `ZSTD_c_maxBlockSize` (`experimentalParam18`) | 1015 | `[1024, 131072]` | default 131072 | block size cap; also changes `maxNbSeq`, workspace |\n| `ZSTD_c_repcodeResolution` / `ZSTD_c_searchForExternalRepcodes` (`experimentalParam19`) | 1016 | `[0, 2]` | auto = `cLevel<10 ? disable : enable` | repcode search for external sequences |\n| `ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel` (`experimentalParam20`) | 1017 | `[0, 6]` (`ZSTD_BLOCKSPLITTER_LEVEL_MAX=6`) | 0 = strategy-derived | 1 → never presplit; 2..6 → `ZSTD_splitBlock(level-2)` ∈ 0..4. Strategy default map `splitLevels[] = {0,0,1,2,2,3,3,4,4,4}` indexed by strategy |\n\nAlso `ZSTD_CCtx_setCParams` / `setFParams` / `setParams` take whole structs; `ZSTD_CCtxParams_init(level)` and `ZSTD_CCtxParams_init_advanced(ZSTD_parameters)` resolve auto values eagerly.\n\n## 2.3 All `ZSTD_dParameter`\n\n| enum | value | bounds | 0 means | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ZSTD_d_windowLogMax` | 100 | `[10, 31]` | `ZSTD_WINDOWLOG_LIMIT_DEFAULT = 27` | `maxWindowSize = 1<<v`; frames with larger window → `frameParameter_windowTooLarge` |\n| `ZSTD_d_format` (`experimentalParam1`) | 1000 | `[0, 1]` | zstd1 | magicless decoding |\n| `ZSTD_d_stableOutBuffer` (`experimentalParam2`) | 1001 | `[0, 1]` | buffered | decompress directly into caller buffer |\n| `ZSTD_d_forceIgnoreChecksum` (`experimentalParam3`) | 1002 | `[0, 1]` validateChecksum/ignoreChecksum | validate | skip XXH check |\n| `ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts` (`experimentalParam4`) | 1003 | `[0, 1]` refSingleDDict/refMultipleDDicts | single | dictID-keyed DDict set; **errors on static DCtx** |\n| `ZSTD_d_disableHuffmanAssembly` (`experimentalParam5`) | 1004 | `[0, 1]` | off | forces C huffman decode loops |\n| `ZSTD_d_maxBlockSize` (`experimentalParam6`) | 1005 | `0` or `[1024, 131072]` | default 131072 | rejects frames with larger blockSizeMax |\n| — | — | — | — | `ZSTD_DCtx_setMaxWindowSize(size)`: `size ∈ [1<<10, 1<<31]`, requires `streamStage == zdss_init` |\n\nNote: **every** `ZSTD_DCtx_setParameter` call errors with `stage_wrong` unless the DCtx is at `zdss_init` (i.e. right after create/reset).\n\n## 2.4 Frame-format toggles (numeric summary)\n`ZSTD_MAGICNUMBER=0xFD2FB528`, `ZSTD_MAGIC_DICTIONARY=0xEC30A437`, `ZSTD_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START=0x184D2A50` (mask `0xFFFFFFF0`, variants 0..15), `ZSTD_SKIPPABLEHEADERSIZE=8`, `ZSTD_FRAMEHEADERSIZE_PREFIX=5` (zstd1) / `1` (magicless), `_MIN=6`/`2`, `_MAX=18`, `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZELOG_MAX=17`, `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX=131072`, `ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX_MIN=1024`, `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN=(U64)-1`, `ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR=(U64)-2`.\n\n## 2.5 Input SHAPES\n| name | concrete bytes |\n|---|---|\n| empty | 0 |\n| one byte | 1 (`'A'`) |\n| tiny | 7, 13 |\n| sub-block | 1000, 8191, 65536 |\n| exactly one block | **131072** (`ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`) |\n| block+1 | 131073 |\n| multi-block | 262144, 400000, 1048576 |\n| larger than window (forces wrap/extDict) | with `windowLog=10` → 4096 bytes; with `windowLog=17` → 300000 bytes |\n| highly compressible | `\"abcdefgh\"` repeated to N |\n| incompressible (raw blocks) | LCG/`rand()` pseudo-random bytes, N = 1000 / 131072 / 300000 |\n| RLE-able | all `0x00` (or all `0x5A`) — triggers `ZSTD_isRLE` → `bt_rle` block; test N = 1, 33, 131072 |\n| text-like | repeated English/Lorem-ipsum corpus 300000 bytes |\n| near-RLE | 131072 bytes of one value with 3 sequences / <10 literals (`ZSTD_maybeRLE`) |\n| pledgedSrcSize | unknown (`ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN`) vs exact vs **wrong** (too big / too small → `srcSize_wrong`) vs 0 |\n\n## 2.6 Streaming shapes\n- input chunk sizes: **1, 2, 7, 100, 1000, 4096, 131072, ZSTD_CStreamInSize()**\n- output chunk sizes: **1, 2, 7, 100, 1000, ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()**, and exactly-large-enough\n- decompress out chunk: **1, 7, 1000, 131072, ZSTD_DStreamOutSize()**\n- end directives: `ZSTD_e_continue=0`, `ZSTD_e_flush=1`, `ZSTD_e_end=2`; interleaving patterns: all-continue-then-end; flush every chunk; flush at byte 1; end with empty input; e_end called repeatedly until 0\n- old API: `ZSTD_compressStream` + `ZSTD_flushStream` + `ZSTD_endStream`; `ZSTD_resetCStream(pledged)`; `ZSTD_initCStream_srcSize(level, srcSize)`\n- reset directives: `ZSTD_reset_session_only=1`, `ZSTD_reset_parameters=2`, `ZSTD_reset_session_and_parameters=3` (`reset_parameters` errors mid-frame)\n\n## 2.7 Multi-frame / skippable / magicless\n- 2 and 3 concatenated zstd frames (same and different levels/checksum flags)\n- skippable frame before / between / after real frames; magic variants **0, 1, 7, 15**; payload sizes **0, 1, 8, 1000**\n- skippable frame with content size field larger than remaining input (error path)\n- magicless: compress with `ZSTD_c_format=1`, decompress with `ZSTD_d_format=1`; also cross-mismatch (magicless data + zstd1 decoder → error)\n- multi-frame where a later frame has unknown content size (`ZSTD_findDecompressedSize` → `CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN`, `ZSTD_decompressBound` still finite)\n\n## 2.8 Dictionary shapes\n- **no dict**\n- **raw-content dict**: arbitrary buffer (no magic), sizes 0, 1, 8, 256, 8192, 112640 (>frame window)\n- **trained dict**: from `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` (starts with `0xEC30A437`, has dictID + entropy tables)\n- **prefix**: `ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix` / `ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix` (single-use, raw content by default)\n- `ZSTD_dictLoadMethod_e`: `ZSTD_dlm_byCopy=0`, `ZSTD_dlm_byRef=1`\n- `ZSTD_dictContentType_e`: `ZSTD_dct_auto=0`, `ZSTD_dct_rawContent=1`, `ZSTD_dct_fullDict=2` (fullDict on a raw buffer → `dictionary_corrupted`)\n- attach vs copy vs load: `ZSTD_dictAttachPref_e` `{0 default, 1 forceAttach, 2 forceCopy, 3 forceLoad}`; the default heuristic (`ZSTD_shouldAttachDict`) attaches when `pledgedSrcSize <= attachDictSizeCutoffs[strategy]` (`{unused 8K, fast 8K, dfast 16K, greedy 32K, lazy 32K, lazy2 32K, …}`) **or** pledged size unknown, and `!forceWindow`\n- dedicated dict search: `ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch=1` with `greedy/lazy/lazy2` + `hashLog>chainLog` + `chainLog≤24`\n- decoder side: `ZSTD_DCtx_refDDict` with `ZSTD_rmd_refSingleDDict` vs `ZSTD_rmd_refMultipleDDicts` and 2 DDicts of different dictIDs\n- wrong dict on decompress → `dictionary_wrong`; `dictIDFlag=0` compression then dict-less decode\n- `ZSTD_createCDict_advanced2` with a `ZSTD_CCtx_params` (level and cParams from params, `ZSTD_cpm_createCDict` mode)\n- static allocations: `ZSTD_initStaticCDict`, `ZSTD_initStaticDDict`, `ZSTD_initStaticCCtx/DCtx/CStream/DStream` with exactly-estimated and one-byte-short workspaces\n\n## 2.9 dictBuilder axes\nCommon `ZDICT_params_t`: `compressionLevel ∈ {0(→3), 1, 3, 9, 19}`, `notificationLevel = 0` (keep 0 to avoid stderr), `dictID ∈ {0 (random — non-deterministic, must be pinned!), 1, 12345, 0x80000001}`.\n**Important for differential testing: pin `dictID` to a non-zero constant**, because `dictID==0` draws a random 32-bit value.\n\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer`: fixed d=8, steps=4, level=3 → `optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover`\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover`: `k ∈ {16, 50, 200, 1000, 2048}`, `d ∈ {6, 8, 16}` with `d ≤ k`, `splitPoint ∈ {0 (→1.0), 0.5, 0.75, 1.0}`, `nbThreads` ignored, `shrinkDict ∈ {0,1}`, `shrinkDictMaxRegression ∈ {0, 1, 5}`. Validation: `d!=0 && k!=0 && k<=maxDictSize && d<=k && 0<splitPoint<=1`\n- `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover`: `k=0,d=0` → sweeps `d ∈ {6,8}`, `k ∈ [50, 2000]` step `max((2000-50)/steps,1)`; `steps ∈ {0(→40), 1, 4, 8}`; default splitPoint `1.0`\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover`: `f ∈ {0(→20), 1, 6, 20, 25, 31}` (`FASTCOVER_MAX_F=31`), `accel ∈ {0(→1), 1, 2, 5, 10}` (`FASTCOVER_MAX_ACCEL=10`, table `{100/0, 100/0, 50/1, 34/2, 25/3, 20/4, 17/5, 14/6, 13/7, 11/8, 10/9}`), splitPoint forced to `1.0` in the non-optimize path, `k`/`d` as cover\n- `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover`: default splitPoint `0.75`, `shrinkDict` forced 0, sweeps as above\n- `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy`: `selectivityLevel ∈ {0(→9), 1, 5, 9, 12, 31}`; requires `samplesBuffSize >= ZDICT_MIN_SAMPLES_SIZE = 128*4 = 512`, `MINRATIO=4`\n- `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary`: `maxDictSize ∈ {256 (ZDICT_DICTSIZE_MIN), 1024, 8192, dictContentSize}`; dictContent = raw buffer, and dictContent overlapping dstDictBuffer; `maxDictSize < max(dictContentSize, 256)` → error\n- `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer` (deprecated wrapper)\n- `ZDICT_getDictID`, `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize` on: valid trained dict, raw buffer, 3-byte buffer\n- Failure shapes to exercise: 0 samples, 1 sample, all-identical samples, incompressible samples, total sample size < 512\n\n## 2.10 Entropy / hash / pool axes\n- **FSE**: `FSE_MAX_TABLELOG = FSE_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE-2 = 12`, `FSE_DEFAULT_TABLELOG = 11`, `FSE_MIN_TABLELOG = 5`, `FSE_TABLELOG_ABSOLUTE_MAX = 15`, `FSE_NCOUNTBOUND = 512`. tableLog values to test: **5, 6, 9, 11, 12** (and 13 → error). `maxSymbolValue ∈ {1, 2, 15, 100, 255}`. `useLowProbCount ∈ {0,1}` in `FSE_normalizeCount`. `FSE_optimalTableLog(maxTableLog, srcSize, maxSymbolValue)` and `_internal(..., minus ∈ {0,1,2})`. `FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2(..., maxLog, ..., bmi2 ∈ {0,1})` (bmi2 has no effect at DYNAMIC_BMI2=0).\n- **HUF**: `HUF_TABLELOG_MAX = 12`, `HUF_TABLELOG_DEFAULT = 11`, `HUF_TABLELOG_ABSOLUTEMAX = 12`, `HUF_SYMBOLVALUE_MAX = 255`, `HUF_BLOCKSIZE_MAX = 131072`, `HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE = 8704`. `huffLog ∈ {5, 8, 11, 12}`. `flags` bitmask: `HUF_flags_bmi2=1`, `optimalDepth=2`, `preferRepeat=4`, `suspectUncompressible=8`, `disableAsm=16`, `disableFast=32` — test `0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 48, 63`. `HUF_repeat ∈ {none=0, check=1, valid=2}`. 1-stream (`1X`) vs 4-stream (`4X`); X1 (single-symbol) vs X2 (double-symbol) DTables via `HUF_selectDecoder`.\n- **XXH32/XXH64**: one-shot `ZSTD_XXH32/64(buf, len, seed)` and streaming `reset(seed)`+N×`update`+`digest`. lengths: **0, 1, 3, 4, 7, 8, 15, 16, 31, 32, 33, 63, 64, 127, 128, 1000, 131072**; seeds: **0, 1, 0x9E3779B1, 0xFFFFFFFF** (32) and **0, 1, 0x27D4EB2F165667C5ULL, UINT64_MAX** (64); streaming chunk splits: 1, 3, 7, 16, 1000; `copyState` mid-stream; `canonicalFromHash` / `hashFromCanonical` round-trips.\n- **POOL** (non-MT stubs): `POOL_create(numThreads, queueSize)` with `numThreads ∈ {0, 1, 2, 4, 16}` × `queueSize ∈ {0, 1, 4}`; `POOL_create_advanced` with default and custom `ZSTD_customMem`; `POOL_add` (runs job synchronously), `POOL_tryAdd` (returns 1), `POOL_resize(ctx, n)` for `n ∈ {0,1,4}` (returns 0), `POOL_sizeof` (returns 0), `POOL_joinJobs`, `POOL_free(NULL)`.\n\n---\n\n# SECTION 3 — Pruned cross-product test matrix\n\nNotes that apply to the whole table:\n- **The repo contains no legacy-format (v0.1–v0.7) sample data** — no `.zst` fixtures anywhere under `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-gwFUqA`. The legacy decoders therefore have to be exercised (a) on hand-built buffers carrying the right magic (`0xFD2FB51E/22/23/24/25/26/27` LE) and truncated/mutated bodies, (b) on modern zstd frames (must be rejected with `prefix_unknown`), and (c) on random/zero/1-byte buffers. None of the seven legacy files contain an *encoder*, so no legacy frames can be produced in-tree; only error/`isError`/`findFrameSizeInfoLegacy`/`nextSrcSizeToDecompress` paths and `ZSTD_isLegacy`-dispatch behaviour are differentially observable.\n- `ZDICT_*` calls must pin `zParams.dictID` to a non-zero constant, else output is randomized.\n- `prefetchCDictTables` and `HUF_flags_bmi2/disableAsm` must not change bytes — assert identical output as a stronger property.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 1 (→ZSTD_fast), text-like 300000 B |\n| 2 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 3 (→ZSTD_dfast), text-like 300000 B |\n| 3 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 5 (→ZSTD_greedy), text-like 300000 B |\n| 4 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 6 (→ZSTD_lazy), text-like 300000 B |\n| 5 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 9 (→ZSTD_lazy2), text-like 300000 B |\n| 6 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 13 (→ZSTD_btlazy2), text-like 300000 B |\n| 7 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 16 (→ZSTD_btopt), text-like 300000 B |\n| 8 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 18 (→ZSTD_btultra), text-like 300000 B |\n| 9 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` / `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | level 19 (→ZSTD_btultra2), text-like 300000 B |\n| 10 | `ZSTD_compress` | level 22, text-like 300000 B |\n| 11 | `ZSTD_compress` | level -1 (row 0, targetLength=1), incompressible 131072 B |\n| 12 | `ZSTD_compress` | level -5, highly compressible 262144 B |\n| 13 | `ZSTD_compress` | level -131072 (= `ZSTD_minCLevel()`), random 131072 B |\n| 14 | `ZSTD_compress` | level 0 (→3) and level 3 — assert identical output; 1000 B text |\n| 15 | `ZSTD_compress` | level 100 (out of range, clamped to 22) vs level 22 — assert identical; 65536 B |\n| 16 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=1 `ZSTD_fast`, level 6, windowLog 20, text 300000 B |\n| 17 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=2 `ZSTD_dfast`, level 6, text 300000 B |\n| 18 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=3 `ZSTD_greedy`, `useRowMatchFinder=1(enable)`, windowLog 20, text 300000 B |\n| 19 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=3 `ZSTD_greedy`, `useRowMatchFinder=2(disable)`, windowLog 20, text 300000 B |\n| 20 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=4 `ZSTD_lazy`, `useRowMatchFinder=0(auto)`, windowLog **14** (→auto disable) vs **15** (→auto enable), text 300000 B |\n| 21 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=5 `ZSTD_lazy2`, `useRowMatchFinder=1`, text 300000 B |\n| 22 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=6 `ZSTD_btlazy2`, text 300000 B |\n| 23 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=7 `ZSTD_btopt`, `targetLength=48`, `minMatch=3`, text 300000 B |\n| 24 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=8 `ZSTD_btultra`, `targetLength=999`, text 300000 B |\n| 25 | `ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_strategy` | strategy=9 `ZSTD_btultra2`, `targetLength=0`, text 300000 B |\n| 26 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `windowLog=10` (min) + input 4096 B (forces window wrap / extDict) |\n| 27 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `windowLog=17`, input 300000 B (multi-window wrap, strategy=lazy2) |\n| 28 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `windowLog=31` (max), input 1000 B; then decode with `ZSTD_d_windowLogMax=31` and with default 27 (→`frameParameter_windowTooLarge`) |\n| 29 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `hashLog=6` (min) and `hashLog=25`, strategy=fast, 131072 B |\n| 30 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `chainLog=6` (min) and `chainLog=25`, strategy=lazy2 + rowMF disabled, 262144 B |\n| 31 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `searchLog=1` (min) and `searchLog=12`, strategy=btopt, 262144 B |\n| 32 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `minMatch=3`, strategy=btultra, 262144 B |\n| 33 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `minMatch=7`, strategy=fast, 262144 B |\n| 34 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `minMatch=4,5,6`, strategy=greedy, 262144 B |\n| 35 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `targetLength=0`, `1`, `131072` (max), strategy=btopt, 262144 B |\n| 36 | `ZSTD_compress2` | `contentSizeFlag=0` vs `1`, pledgedSrcSize known, 65536 B — header FCS fiel