hist_functions` (row 203): HIST_count, HIST_count_simple, HIST_count_wksp, HIST_countFast, HIST_countFast_wksp, HIST_add, HIST_isError. Compare both the return value AND the full count[] array and the written maxSymbolValuePtr. Use maxSymbolValue ∈ {1,15,255} × src ∈ {empty, 1 byte, 4096 all-one-byte, 4096 random, 4096 text}. Get exact signatures from c_src/src/compress/hist.h.\n- `fse_roundtrip` (rows 204, 205): full pipeline HIST_count -> FSE_normalizeCount(useLowProbCount 0 and 1) -> FSE_writeNCount -> FSE_buildCTable_wksp -> FSE_compress_usingCTable -> FSE_readNCount / FSE_readNCount_bmi2(bmi2 0 and 1) -> FSE_buildDTable_wksp -> FSE_decompress_wksp_bmi2. Compare every intermediate buffer byte-for-byte and every return code. tableLog ∈ {5,6,9,11,12} plus 13 (must error identically), maxSymbolValue ∈ {1,15,100,255}, src = text/random/skewed(99% one symbol) 4096 B. Also FSE_buildCTable_rle(sym ∈ {0,127,255}) + FSE_compress_usingCTable. Exact signatures/workspace sizes are in c_src/src/common/fse.h (look for FSE_BUILD_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE_U32, FSE_DTABLE_SIZE_U32, FSE_DECOMPRESS_WKSP_SIZE_U32, FSE_CTABLE_SIZE_U32 macros) — compute workspace sizes in Rust to match.\n- `huf_roundtrip` (rows 206, 207, 209): HUF_optimalTableLog, HUF_buildCTable_wksp, HUF_writeCTable_wksp, HUF_compress4X_usingCTable, HUF_compress1X_usingCTable, HUF_readDTableX1_wksp, HUF_readDTableX2_wksp, HUF_decompress4X_usingDTable, HUF_decompress1X_usingDTable, HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress1X_DCtx_wksp, HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly_wksp. huffLog ∈ {5,8,11,12}; flags ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,16,32,48,63}; src text/random 4096 and 131072 B. Signatures + HUF_WORKSPACE_SIZE etc. in c_src/src/common/huf.h.\n- `huf_repeat` (row 208): HUF_compress4X_repeat and HUF_compress1X_repeat with *repeat ∈ {0 none,1 check,2 valid} across 3 successive blocks (similar then dissimilar data); compare the updated repeat value too.\n- `huf_helpers` (row 210): HUF_minTableLog, HUF_cardinality, HUF_validateCTable, HUF_estimateCompressedSize, HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable, HUF_readCTable, HUF_readCTableHeader, HUF_selectDecoder, HUF_readStats, HUF_readStats_wksp, HUF_compressBound, HUF_isError, HUF_getErrorName — on the CTable from huf_roundtrip and on random 128 B input.\n- `xxh32`, `xxh64` (rows 211, 212): ZSTD_XXH32 / ZSTD_XXH64 one-shot over lengths {0,1,3,4,7,8,15,16,31,32,33,63,64,127,128,1000,131072} × seeds {0,1,0x9E3779B1,0xFFFFFFFF} / {0,1,0x27D4EB2F165667C5,u64::MAX}.\n- `xxh32_stream`, `xxh64_stream` (rows 213, 214): ZSTD_XXH{32,64}_createState/reset/update/digest/copyState/freeState, chunk splits {1,3,7,16,1000} over 4096 and 131072 B, update(NULL,0), copyState halfway then digest both.\n- `xxh_canonical` (row 215): ZSTD_XXH{32,64}_canonicalFromHash + _hashFromCanonical round trips, ZSTD_XXH_versionNumber.\n- `pool_basic`, `pool_advanced`, `pool_jobs` (rows 216-218): POOL_create(numThreads ∈ {0,1,2,4,16} × queueSize ∈ {0,1,4}), POOL_free(NULL), POOL_create_advanced with default ZSTD_customMem{null,null,null} and a custom allocator pair implemented in Rust (`extern \"C\" fn`), mismatched alloc/free (alloc set, free NULL) must return NULL in both, POOL_add / POOL_tryAdd (job = extern \"C\" fn incrementing an AtomicUsize) with 0/1/5 jobs, POOL_joinJobs, POOL_resize(0/1/4), POOL_sizeof. Compare return values and observable side effects. NOTE: the library is compiled WITHOUT ZSTD_MULTITHREAD, so POOL_* are synchronous stubs — verify both behave the same; do NOT assume threads run.\n\nRULES:\n- Only create/modify `tests/phase_b_entropy.rs`. Do NOT touch c_src/, SYMBOLS.md, ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md, other tests, or Cargo.toml.\n- Verify every symbol you use exists: `nm -D --defined-only ../c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep NAME`.\n- Get exact C signatures by reading the headers in c_src/src/common/ (fse.h, huf.h, xxhash.h, pool.h) and c_src/src/compress/hist.h. Match types exactly (unsigned = c_uint, size_t = usize, void* = *mut c_void, int = c_int).\n- Use a fixed 