{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a5f08e7a2d398c344","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018ta38GmxYRrD5CPxbp4xUZ","description":"Write dictBuilder differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are writing ONE new Rust integration test file in an existing crate. Work dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-gwFUqA/translation\n\nContext: `c_src/build/libzstd.so` (C, ground truth) and `translation/target/release/libzstd.so` (Rust port) are both built. Existing harness `tests/common/mod.rs` loads BOTH .so files via libloading and exposes:\n  `pair::<FnType>(\"SYMBOL\") -> (Symbol<'static,FnType>, Symbol<'static,FnType>)` (C first, Rust second),\n  `Rng::new(seed)` with `.below(n)/.range(lo,hi)/.byte()/.next_u32()`,\n  `gen(Shape, len, &mut rng)`, `Shape::{Random,Rle,Repetitive,Text,LongMatches,Mixed,Sparse}`, `ALL_SHAPES`,\n  `assert_bytes_eq(ctx,&c,&r)`, `is_error(code)`, `err_code(code)`.\nRead tests/common/mod.rs and tests/phase_b_dict.rs first for the established style.\n\nYOUR TASK: create `tests/phase_b_dictbuilder.rs` covering the dictBuilder API differentially (C vs Rust must produce BYTE-IDENTICAL dictionaries and identical error codes). Use these EXACT test function names (they are referenced by CONFIGS.md / ERRORS.md):\n\n`dictb_train_basic` (row 185), `dictb_train_edge` (186), `dictb_cover` (187,188), `err_dictb_cover_params` (189, ERRORS 290-299), `dictb_cover_optimize` (190,191), `dictb_fastcover` (192,193), `err_dictb_fastcover_params` (194, ERRORS 300-308), `dictb_fastcover_optimize` (195), `dictb_legacy` (196), `err_dictb_legacy` (ERRORS 309-312), `dictb_finalize` (197,199), `err_dictb_finalize` (198, ERRORS 282-286, 313), `dictb_queries` (200, ERRORS 278-280), `err_dictb_headersize` (ERRORS 281), `err_dictb_train` (ERRORS 287-289), `dictb_cover_internals` (201).\n\nEntry points (verify each with `nm -D --defined-only ../c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep NAME`; read exact signatures + struct layouts from c_src/src/include/zdict.h and c_src/src/dictBuilder/cover.h):\n- ZDICT_trainFromBuffer(dictBuffer, dictBufferCapacity, samplesBuffer, samplesSizes, nbSamples)\n- ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover(..., ZDICT_cover_params_t) and ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover(..., *mut ZDICT_cover_params_t) — ALSO compare the params struct written back by the optimize variants\n- ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover(..., ZDICT_fastCover_params_t), ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover(..., *mut ...)\n- ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy(..., ZDICT_legacy_params_t)\n- ZDICT_finalizeDictionary(dstDictBuffer, maxDictSize, dictContent, dictContentSize, samplesBuffer, samplesSizes, nbSamples, ZDICT_params_t)\n- ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer, ZDICT_getDictID, ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize, ZDICT_isError, ZDICT_getErrorName (compare the C strings)\n- COVER_computeEpochs, COVER_sum, COVER_best_init/start/wait/finish/destroy, COVER_selectDict, COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize, COVER_dictSelectionError/Free/IsError, COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus, divsufsort, divbwt (signatures in cover.h / divsufsort.h). For `dictb_cover_internals` at minimum exercise COVER_computeEpochs (maxDictSize ∈ {256,8192} × nbDmers × k × passes ∈ {1,4}), COVER_sum, and divsufsort/divbwt on 4096 B text and 4096 B all-zero input (compare the whole output arrays).\n\nCRITICAL correctness notes:\n- `ZDICT_params_t.dictID == 0` makes the C code choose a RANDOM dictID, so output is nondeterministic. ALWAYS pin dictID to a non-zero constant (e.g. 1, 12345, 0x80000001) when comparing bytes. You may still test dictID=0 but then only compare return values, not bytes.\n- Keep `notificationLevel = 0` to avoid stderr noise.\n- Parameter ranges/limits to sweep: cover k ∈ {16,50,200,1000,2048}, d ∈ {6,8,16} (d<=k), splitPoint ∈ {0.0(→1.0),0.5,0.75,1.0}, shrinkDict ∈ {0,1}, shrinkDictMaxRegression ∈ {0,1,5}, steps ∈ {0(→40),1,4,8}, nbThreads ∈ {1,4}; fastCover f ∈ {0(→20),1,6,20,25,31} and f=32 (invalid), accel ∈ {0(→1),1,2,5,10} and 11 (invalid); legacy selectivityLevel ∈ {0(→9),1,5,9,12,31}; compressionLevel ∈ {0(→3),1,3,9,19}; dictBufferCapacity ∈ {100(too small),256,1024,4096,16384,112640}.\n- Invalid-parameter tests must assert C and Rust return the SAME error code (compare the exact size_t), not merely \"both failed\".\n- Build training corpora with `gen(Shape::Text, ...)` (~200-400 samples of 64-512 B) and also incompressible (Shape::Random) and all-identical samples; also 0 samples, 1 sample, and a corpus whose total size is 511 bytes (< the 512 B minimum).\n\nRULES:\n- Only create/modify `tests/phase_b_dictbuilder.rs`. Do NOT touch c_src/, SYMBOLS.md, ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md, other test files, or Cargo.toml.\n- Fixed seeds; several randomized corpora per configuration.\n- Run `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_dictbuilder` and iterate until ALL tests pass (`--offline` is REQUIRED, there is no network). Some optimize/cover runs are slow — keep corpora modest (<= 300 KB total) so the whole file runs in a few minutes.\n- If C and Rust genuinely diverge, first re-check your struct layout (field order/types!) and dictID pinning. If it is a real translation bug you MAY fix translation/src/ to match the C, and must report exactly what you changed.\n- Report: test function names, final cargo test summary line, and any divergences found/fixed.","uuid":"eb4859ea-413a-4414-b6bf-d605854ae33b","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a"}
