sInitDictionary mid-compression must return the same stage_wrong error.\n- `err_zbuff_forwarding` (ERRORS 276,277): ZBUFF_compressContinue/Flush/End and ZBUFF_decompressContinue with a too-small dst buffer, and ZBUFF_decompressContinue on corrupt/truncated input and on a buffer with an unknown magic — assert identical error codes.\nNOTE: the ZBUFF API uses `size_t*` in/out size pointers, e.g. `size_t ZBUFF_compressContinue(ZBUFF_CCtx*, void* dst, size_t* dstCapacityPtr, const void* src, size_t* srcSizePtr)`. Read zbuff.h for the exact signatures and compare the values written back through those pointers too.\n\nFILE 2: `tests/phase_b_legacy.rs` — the legacy v0.1..v0.7 decoders (headers c_src/src/legacy/zstd_v0*.h, zstd_legacy.h). EXACT test names `legacy_v01`, `legacy_v02`, `legacy_v03`, `legacy_v04`, `legacy_v05`, `legacy_v06`, `legacy_v07`, `legacy_entropy`, `legacy_isError`.\nThere is NO legacy-format sample data in the repo and no legacy encoder, so exercise the decoders on hand-built buffers and assert C and Rust return IDENTICAL codes / outputs for each:\n  (a) the correct 4-byte magic alone (v01 0xFD2FB51E, v02 ...522, v03 ...523, v04 ...524, v05 ...525, v06 ...526, v07 ...527 — verify the magic constants in the headers, note v01/v02/v03 read the magic in a specific endianness),\n  (b) magic + 64/256 bytes of deterministic pseudo-random garbage,\n  (c) magic + a plausible but corrupt frame header/block header,\n  (d) a modern zstd frame (produced with ZSTD_compress) fed to each legacy decoder,\n  (e) buffers of 0, 1, 3, 4, 5 bytes,\n  (f) 1024 all-zero bytes.\nFor each version call every exported entry point of that version: ZSTDvXX_decompress, _decompressDCtx, createDCtx/freeDCtx, resetDCtx (v01-v04), nextSrcSizeToDecompress, decompressContinue, isError, findFrameSizeInfoLegacy (compare BOTH out params cSize/dBound), plus the extra v05/v06/v07 entry points (getFrameParams — compare the whole out struct, decompressBegin(_usingDict), decompressBlock, decompress_usingDict, decompress_usingPreparedDCtx (v05), copyDCtx, sizeofDCtx, and for v07 createDDict/freeDDict/decompress_usingDDict/insertBlock/isSkipFrame/getDecompressedSize/estimateDCtxSize/createDCtx_advanced) and the ZBUFFv04/v05/v06/v07 entry points. Get exact signatures and struct layouts from the legacy headers; the params structs differ per version.\n`legacy_entropy` (CONFIGS 183,184): FSEv05/v06/v07_* and HUFv05/v06/v07_* exported symbols — createDTable(tableLog ∈ {5,9,11,12}), buildDTable_raw(nbBits ∈ {1,4,8}), buildDTable_rle(sym ∈ {0,127,255}), readNCount on random 64 B, decompress/_usingDTable on random and all-zero 256 B, freeDTable, isError, getErrorName; HUF readDTableX2/X4 on random 128 B, decompress/1X2/1X4/4X2/4X4 (+_usingDTable, +_DCtx for v07), HUFv07_readStats, HUFv07_selectDecoder, HUFv07_decompress4X_hufOnly on random and all-zero 512 B. Compare return codes AND output buffers.\n`legacy_isError`: every ZSTDvXX_isError on 0, 1, (size_t)-1, (size_t)-10, (size_t)-72, (size_t)-120, (size_t)-121.\nAlso test `ZSTD_isFrame` and `ZSTD_decompress` on each legacy magic buffer (auto-dispatch: only v05/v06/v07 are dispatched since ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5) — assert identical results.\n\nRULES:\n- Only create/modify `tests/phase_b_zbuff.rs` and `tests/phase_b_legacy.rs`. Do NOT touch c_src/, SYMBOLS.md, ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md, other test files, or Cargo.toml.\n- Verify each symbol exists: `nm -D --defined-only ../c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep NAME`. The full list is in ../scratch/c_syms.txt.\n- IMPORTANT: never dereference or free a pointer one library returned using the other library. Keep C objects with C functions and Rust objects with Rust functions.\n- Use fixed seeds and several randomized buffers per case.\n- Run `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_zbuff` and `... --test phase_b_legacy` and iterate until ALL tests pass (`--offline` is REQUIRED, no network).\n- If C and Rust genuinely diverge (double-check your signatures/struct layouts first), you MAY fix translation/src/ to match the C, and must report exactly what you changed.\n- Report: test names per file, the final cargo test summary lines, and any divergences found/fixed.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-yeqFPb/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-gwFUqA/2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a/tasks/a44569c692d595e67.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
