ix length 0..min(len,40) plus len-1, len/2), a non-frame random buffer.\n- `cfg_decompression_margin` (119): ZSTD_decompressionMargin on single frame with/without checksum and multi-frame input; then perform an in-place decompression using the returned margin and compare the output.\n- `cfg_isframe_isskippable` (120, ERRORS 208,209): ZSTD_isFrame and ZSTD_isSkippableFrame on: a zstd frame, all 16 skippable magics 0x184D2A50..0x184D2A5F, the legacy magics 0xFD2FB51E/522/523/524/525/526/527, a magicless frame, buffers of 0/1/3/4 bytes, random buffers.\n- `cfg_skippable_roundtrip` (121): ZSTD_writeSkippableFrame + ZSTD_readSkippableFrame with magicVariant ∈ {0,1,7,15} × payload sizes {0,1,8,1000}; compare bytes, the returned magicVariant out-param, and the return codes.\n- `err_skippable` (ERRORS 115,117,164,203-207): writeSkippableFrame with dstCapacity = srcSize+7 (too small) and magicVariant 16/99/u32::MAX; readSkippableFrame with srcSize<8, wrong magic, declared size > srcSize, payload > dstCapacity. Assert identical error codes.\n- `cfg_decompress_concat_skippable` (122): ZSTD_decompress on [skippable][frame][skippable][frame][skippable] with varying payloads.\n- `cfg_bound_functions` (161): ZSTD_compressBound, ZSTD_decompressBound, ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min over sizes {0,1,131072,1<<20,1<<30,usize::MAX/2} (and for decodingBufferSize_min: windowSize/blockSize combinations incl. huge values that must return the same error — see ERRORS 259).\n- `err_decompression_margin` (ERRORS 202) and `err_findframecompressedsize` (ERRORS 197-200) and `err_contentsize_queries` (ERRORS 190-196,201): construct each condition (truncated header, bad magic, windowLog field 32, checksum flag with <4 bytes remaining, skippable frame with declared size > input, unknown-FCS frame, huge declared FCS) and assert identical returns.\n- `err_frameheader_queries` (ERRORS 186-189): ZSTD_frameHeaderSize and ZSTD_getFrameHeader(_advanced) with srcSize below the minimum, src=NULL with srcSize>0, unknown magic, and every truncation of a valid header.\n\nFILE 2: `tests/phase_b_seq.rs` — the sequence API. EXACT test names:\n- `cfg_generate_sequences` (146): ZSTD_sequenceBound over sizes {0,1,1000,131072,300000}; ZSTD_generateSequences at levels {1,5,9,19} on text/random/repetitive inputs of 1000/131072/300000 B. Compare the returned count AND the whole ZSTD_Sequence array (4 u32 fields: offset, litLength, matchLength, rep).\n- `err_generateSequences_targetCBlockSize` (ERRORS 119,120) and `err_generateSequences_capacity` (ERRORS 121): targetCBlockSize != 0 / nbWorkers != 0 on the cctx, and outSeqsCapacity below ZSTD_sequenceBound → identical error codes.\n- `cfg_compress_sequences` (147-150): ZSTD_generateSequences (+ ZSTD_mergeBlockDelimiters, compare the merged array) then ZSTD_compressSequences with blockDelimiters 0 and 1, validateSequences 0 and 1, repcodeResolution 0/1/2 at levels 5 and 12, checksumFlag/contentSizeFlag on; compare compressed bytes and round-trip decode.\n- `err_sequences_invalid` (ERRORS 125-132) and `err_compressSequences_dst` (ERRORS 122-124): hand-craft invalid sequence arrays (missing delimiter, offset==0 with matchLength!=0, block bigger than blockSizeMax, lengths summing beyond srcSize, offset beyond window, matchLength<3, too many sequences) and too-small dstCapacity; assert identical error codes.\n- `cfg_compress_sequences_and_literals` (151): ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals happy path (explicit block delimiters, litBufCapacity = litSize+8, correct decompressedSize) built from ZSTD_generateSequences output; compare bytes and round-trip.\n- `err_seq_and_literals` (ERRORS 133-143): litCapacity<litSize, noBlockDelimiters, validateSequences=1, checksumFlag=1, inSeqsSize=0, dstCapacity<3, litLength sum > litSize, dstCapacity<blockHeaderSize, incompressible block, leftover literals, wrong decompressedSize — identical error codes.\n- `err_convertBlockSequences` (ERRORS 144): drive ZSTD_convertBlockSequences with nbSequences >= seqStore.maxNbSeq (read c_src/src/compress/zstd_compress.c for its signature) — if it cannot be called meaningfully in isolation, exercise it through ZSTD_compressSequences with an oversized sequence array and say so in a comment.\n- `cfg_literals_functions` (154): ZSTD_noCompressLiterals, ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock, ZSTD_compressLiterals over literal buffers of 0/1/63/1024/131072 B × random/all-one-byte/text × the flag combinations in their signatures (see c_src/src/compress/zstd_compress_literals.h). Compare bytes and returns.\n- `cfg_seqstore_internals` (153): ZSTD_getSeqStore, ZSTD_resetSeqStore, ZSTD_seqToCodes, ZSTD_selectEncodingType, ZSTD_buildCTable, ZSTD_encodeSequences, ZSTD_buildBlockEntropyStats, ZSTD_fseBitCost, ZSTD_crossEntropyCost — drive them on data derived from a real compression at levels 3 and 19. Signatures are in c_src/src/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h and zstd_compress_sequences.h. If a function needs internal state that cannot be safely built from outside, exercise it indirectly and note it in a comment (do NOT fabricate a passing assertion).\n- `cfg_split_block_direct` (155): ZSTD_splitBlock (see c_src/src/compress/zstd_preSplit.h) at levels 0..4 on 131072 B mixed-entropy data, and ZSTD_compressSuperBlock if it can be driven safely.\n\nFILE 3: `tests/phase_b_mem.rs` — sizing / static allocation. EXACT test names:\n- `cfg_estimate_functions` (162): ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize, _usingCParams, _usingCCtxParams, ZSTD_estimateCStreamSize(+2 variants), ZSTD_estimateDCtxSize, ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize, ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize_fromFrame, ZSTD_estimateCDictSize, _advanced, ZSTD_estimateDDictSize over levels {1,3,9,19,22}, cParams from ZSTD_getCParams, dictSize {0,8192,112640}, dictLoadMethod {0,1}.\n- `err_estimate_nbworkers` (ERRORS 89,90): the _usingCCtxParams variants with nbWorkers>0 must return the same error (note: setting nbWorkers>0 itself fails in this non-MT build — verify both libs reject it identically and note it).\n- `err_estimate_dstream_fromframe` (ERRORS 260,261): truncated frame header and a frame whose windowLog field is 31/32.\n- `cfg_init_static` (163-165): ZSTD_initStaticCCtx/CStream/DCtx/DStream/CDict/DDict with an exactly-estimated, 8-byte-aligned workspace; then run a full 65536 B compress/decompress round trip through the static contexts and compare bytes.\n- `err_init_static_small` (ERRORS 24,26,102,212,221), `err_init_static_misaligned` (25,101,211,220), `err_init_static_baddict` (103,222), `err_free_static_cctx` (27), `err_free_static_dctx` (213), `err_static_loaddict` (78), `err_static_refMultipleDDicts` (248), `err_static_dstream_small` (267): construct each condition (workspace one byte short, workspace offset by 1 byte to break alignment, a corrupt dict with ZSTD_dct_fullDict, ZSTD_freeCCtx/freeDCtx on a static context, ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary byCopy on a static CCtx, ZSTD_DCtx_setParameter(ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts=1) on a static DCtx, a static DStream too small for the required buffers) and assert C and Rust return the SAME error code / both NULL.\n- `cfg_sizeof_functions` (166): ZSTD_sizeof_CCtx/DCtx/CStream/DStream/CDict/DDict after create, after a compression, after reset.\n- `err_null_free_and_sizeof` (ERRORS 28,29,104,105,214,215,223,224): all free/sizeof functions with NULL.\n- `cfg_frame_progression` (167): ZSTD_getFrameProgression (compare all struct fields — read the struct from zstd.h), ZSTD_toFlushNow, ZSTD_get1BlockSummary at three points during a 400000 B ZSTD_compressStream2 at level 9.\n- `err_custommem_xor` (ERRORS 23,30,99,210,216,273): ZSTD_createCCtx_advanced / createCStream_advanced / createCCtxParams(?) / createCDict_advanced / createDCtx_advanced / createDStream_advanced / createDDict_advanced / ZBUFF_createCCtx_advanced / ZBUFF_createDCtx_advanced with ZSTD_customMem where customAlloc is set but customFree is NULL (and vice versa) → both must return NULL. Also test a WORKING custom allocator pair implemented as Rust `extern \"C\"` functions and run a round trip through it.\n\nRULES:\n- Only create/modify those three files. Do NOT touch c_src/, SYMBOLS.md, ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md, other test files, or Cargo.toml.\n- Verify each symbol exists: `nm -D --defined-only ../c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep NAME` (full list: ../scratch/c_syms.txt).\n- Never free a pointer from one library with the other library's function.\n- Fixed seeds; MANY randomized inputs per configuration.\n- Run `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_frameinfo` (and the other two) and iterate until ALL tests pass. `--offline` is REQUIRED (no network).\n- If C and Rust genuinely diverge (double-check signatures and struct layouts first), you MAY fix translation/src/ to match the C; report exactly what you changed.\n- Report: test names per file, final cargo test summary lines, and any divergences found/fixed.","uuid":"ea7e8b6a-10cd-40f4-baf1-8020f24df4ea","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a"}
