{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AV5i8Va6bGcGVjWr1wgvCq","type":"tool_result","content":"2725\t *  If pledgedSrcSize > 0, its value must be correct, as it will be written in header, and controlled at the end.\n2726\t *  For the time being, pledgedSrcSize==0 is interpreted as \"srcSize unknown\" for compatibility with older programs,\n2727\t *  but it will change to mean \"empty\" in future version, so use macro ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN instead.\n2728\t * @return : 0, or an error code (which can be tested using ZSTD_isError())\n2729\t *  This prototype will generate compilation warnings.\n2730\t */\n2731\tZSTD_DEPRECATED(\"use ZSTD_CCtx_reset, see zstd.h for detailed instructions\")\n2732\tZSTDLIB_STATIC_API\n2733\tsize_t ZSTD_resetCStream(ZSTD_CStream* zcs, unsigned long long pledgedSrcSize);\n2734\t\n2735\t\n2736\ttypedef struct {\n2737\t    unsigned long long ingested;   /* nb input bytes read and buffered */\n2738\t    unsigned long long consumed;   /* nb input bytes actually compressed */\n2739\t    unsigned long long produced;   /* nb of compressed bytes generated and buffered */\n2740\t    unsigned long long flushed;    /* nb of compressed bytes flushed : not provided; can be tracked from caller side */\n2741\t    unsigned currentJobID;         /* MT only : latest started job nb */\n2742\t    unsigned nbActiveWorkers;      /* MT only : nb of workers actively compressing at probe time */\n2743\t} ZSTD_frameProgression;\n2744\t\n2745\t/* ZSTD_getFrameProgression() :\n2746\t * tells how much data has been ingested (read from input)\n2747\t * consumed (input actually compressed) and produced (output) for current frame.\n2748\t * Note : (ingested - consumed) is amount of input data buffered internally, not yet compressed.\n2749\t * Aggregates progression inside active worker threads.\n2750\t */\n2751\tZSTDLIB_STATIC_API ZSTD_frameProgression ZSTD_getFrameProgression(const ZSTD_CCtx* cctx);\n2752\t\n2753\t/*! ZSTD_toFlushNow() :\n2754\t *  Tell how many bytes are ready to be flushed immediately.\n2755\t *  Useful for multithreading scenarios (nbWorkers >= 1).\n2756\t *  Probe the oldest active job, defined as oldest job not yet entirely flushed,\n2757\t *  and check its output buffer.\n2758\t * @return : amount of data stored in oldest job and ready to be flushed immediately.\n2759\t *  if @return == 0, it means either :\n2760\t *  + there is no active job (could be checked with ZSTD_frameProgression()), or\n2761\t *  + oldest job is still actively compressing data,\n2762\t *    but everything it has produced has also been flushed so far,\n2763\t *    therefore flush speed is limited by production speed of oldest job\n2764\t *    irrespective of the speed of concurrent (and newer) jobs.\n2765\t */\n2766\tZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_toFlushNow(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx);\n2767\t\n2768\t\n2769\t/*=====   Advanced Streaming decompression functions  =====*/\n2770\t\n2771\t/*!\n2772\t * This function is deprecated, and is equivalent to:\n2773\t *\n2774\t *     ZSTD_DCtx_reset(zds, ZSTD_reset_session_only);\n2775\t *     ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary(zds, dict, dictSize);\n2776\t *\n2777\t * note: no dictionary will be used if dict == NULL or dictSize < 8\n2778\t */\n2779\tZSTD_DEPRECATED(\"use ZSTD_DCtx_reset + ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary, see zstd.h for detailed instructions\")\n2780\tZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict(ZSTD_DStream* zds, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);\n2781\t\n2782\t/*!\n2783\t * This function is deprecated, and is equivalent to:\n2784\t *"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JDS6Ufv671L4hjddpjV1bD","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a","uuid":"096d6389-ac4a-42e0-9c12-250b65528ac9","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:16:05.720Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write frameinfo/seq/mem tests"}
