{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01U74ocJqUhFDE4RTJqmBVR2","type":"tool_result","content":"378\t\n379\t/* provides the minimum logSize to safely represent a distribution */\n380\t/// `FSE_minTableLog()` from `compress/fse_compress.c`.\n381\t///\n382\t/// `BIT_highbit32(maxSymbolValue)` is `31 - __builtin_clz(maxSymbolValue)`, which\n383\t/// is **undefined for `maxSymbolValue == 0`**. GCC lowers it to a bare `bsr`\n384\t/// instruction, and `bsr` leaves its destination register *unmodified* when the\n385\t/// source operand is zero — so the reference build silently reads whatever the\n386\t/// destination register happened to hold. Because `FSE_minTableLog()` is inlined\n387\t/// into two different callers, the leftover register value differs between them,\n388\t/// and both are reachable from the exported API\n389\t/// (`FSE_optimalTableLog{,_internal}()` and `FSE_normalizeCount()` all accept\n390\t/// `maxSymbolValue == 0`). We therefore let each call site pass the value that its\n391\t/// copy of the code actually reads for `clz(maxSymbolValue)`, so that the observable\n392\t/// behaviour matches the reference `libzstd.so` byte for byte instead of merely\n393\t/// being \"reasonable\".\n394\t///\n395\t/// See the disassembly of `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal` and `FSE_normalizeCount`\n396\t/// in `c_src/build/libzstd.so`:\n397\t/// * `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal`: the `bsr` destination still holds\n398\t///   `clz(srcSize - 1)` (as computed for `maxBitsSrc`).\n399\t/// * `FSE_normalizeCount`: the `bsr` destination still holds the low 32 bits of\n400\t///   `total`, which the following `xor $0x1f` turns into `31 ^ (U32)total`.\n401\t///\n402\t/// `clzMaxSymbolValue` must be `ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32(maxSymbolValue)` whenever\n403\t/// `maxSymbolValue != 0`.\n404\tpub(crate) unsafe fn FSE_minTableLog_withClz(\n405\t    srcSize: usize,\n406\t    clzMaxSymbolValue: c_uint,\n407\t) -> c_uint {\n408\t    let minBitsSrc: U32 = ZSTD_highbit32(srcSize as U32).wrapping_add(1);\n409\t    /* BIT_highbit32(mSV) + 2  ==  (31 - clz(mSV)) + 2  ==  33 - clz(mSV) */\n410\t    let minBitsSymbols: U32 = 33u32.wrapping_sub(clzMaxSymbolValue);\n411\t    let minBits: U32 = if minBitsSrc < minBitsSymbols {\n412\t        minBitsSrc\n413\t    } else {\n414\t        minBitsSymbols\n415\t    };\n416\t    minBits\n417\t}\n418\t\n419\t/// The straightforward reading of `FSE_minTableLog()`; only valid for\n420\t/// `maxSymbolValue != 0`.\n421\tpub(crate) unsafe fn FSE_minTableLog(srcSize: usize, maxSymbolValue: c_uint) -> c_uint {\n422\t    FSE_minTableLog_withClz(srcSize, ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32(maxSymbolValue))\n423\t}\n424\t\n425\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n426\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn FSE_optimalTableLog_internal(\n427\t    maxTableLog: c_uint,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Vw3T2VXPmk7ueJw4J26uBW","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a","uuid":"97954ee6-62a8-43d0-903e-61f554119205","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:30:26.676Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write entropy differential tests"}
