{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EijBPTuuJE7C9oFfHb5hEc","type":"tool_result","content":"   Compiling zstd v1.5.7 (/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-gwFUqA/translation)\n    Finished `release` profile [optimized] target(s) in 1.88s\n     Running tests/phase_b_legacy.rs (target/release/deps/phase_b_legacy-3f62318db798d0ea)\n\nrunning 9 tests\ntest legacy_isError ... ok\ntest legacy_entropy ... ok\ntest legacy_v04 ... ok\ntest legacy_v03 ... ok\ntest legacy_v02 ... ok\ntest legacy_v01 ... ok\ntest legacy_v06 ... ok\ntest legacy_v05 ... ok\ntest legacy_v07 ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 9 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.10s","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WfBCFTShmHPteAvSM4LnN5","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a","uuid":"0985e5e7-0c11-47ce-b5a0-67a093dc352e","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:30:44.162Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write ZBUFF and legacy tests"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bbrcw7ng7cjwq6uv35ajpcqpjcp7ty3bc4i2micszarnlihaoipq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TzvhdyMVLJN3UmpTUM2M8T","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-gwFUqA/translation/src/compress/fse_compress.rs","old_string":"/// `BIT_highbit32(maxSymbolValue)` is `31 - __builtin_clz(maxSymbolValue)`, which\n/// is **undefined for `maxSymbolValue == 0`**. GCC lowers it to a bare `bsr`\n/// instruction, and `bsr` leaves its destination register *unmodified* when the\n/// source operand is zero — so the reference build silently reads whatever the\n/// destination register happened to hold. Because `FSE_minTableLog()` is inlined\n/// into two different callers, the leftover register value differs between them,\n/// and both are reachable from the exported API\n/// (`FSE_optimalTableLog{,_internal}()` and `FSE_normalizeCount()` all accept\n/// `maxSymbolValue == 0`). We therefore let each call site pass the value that its\n/// copy of the code actually reads for `clz(maxSymbolValue)`, so that the observable\n/// behaviour matches the reference `libzstd.so` byte for byte instead of merely\n/// being \"reasonable\".\n///\n/// See the disassembly of `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal` and `FSE_normalizeCount`\n/// in `c_src/build/libzstd.so`:\n/// * `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal`: the `bsr` destination still holds\n///   `clz(srcSize - 1)` (as computed for `maxBitsSrc`).\n/// * `FSE_normalizeCount`: the `bsr` destination still holds the low 32 bits of\n///   `total`, which the following `xor $0x1f` turns into `31 ^ (U32)total`.\n///\n/// `clzMaxSymbolValue` must be `ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32(maxSymbolValue)` whenever\n/// `maxSymbolValue != 0`.\npub(crate) unsafe fn FSE_minTableLog_withClz(\n    srcSize: usize,\n    clzMaxSymbolValue: c_uint,\n) -> c_uint {\n    let minBitsSrc: U32 = ZSTD_highbit32(srcSize as U32).wrapping_add(1);\n    /* BIT_highbit32(mSV) + 2  ==  (31 - clz(mSV)) + 2  ==  33 - clz(mSV) */\n    let minBitsSymbols: U32 = 33u32.wrapping_sub(clzMaxSymbolValue);\n    let minBits: U32 = if minBitsSrc < minBitsSymbols {\n        minBitsSrc\n    } else {\n        minBitsSymbols\n    };\n    minBits\n}\n\n/// The straightforward reading of `FSE_minTableLog()`; only valid for\n/// `maxSymbolValue != 0`.\npub(crate) unsafe fn FSE_minTableLog(srcSize: usize, maxSymbolValue: c_uint) -> c_uint {\n    FSE_minTableLog_withClz(srcSize, ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32(maxSymbolValue))\n}","new_string":"/// `BIT_highbit32(maxSymbolValue)` is `31 - __builtin_clz(maxSymbolValue)`, which\n/// is **undefined for `maxSymbolValue == 0`** (and likewise for `srcSize == 0`).\n/// The reference build compiles `ZSTD_highbit32()` as a real, unoptimised call\n/// chain ending in `bsr -0x4(%rbp),%eax ; xor $0x1f,%eax`; `bsr` leaves its\n/// destination untouched for a zero source and `%eax` still holds the argument\n/// (== 0) at that point, so `ZSTD_highbit32(0)` observably evaluates to `0`.\n/// `ZSTD_highbit32()` reproduces that, so this function needs no special case:\n/// `maxSymbolValue == 0` simply yields `minBitsSymbols == 2`.\n///\n/// `maxSymbolValue == 0` is reachable from the exported API\n/// (`FSE_optimalTableLog{,_internal}()` and `FSE_normalizeCount()` all accept it).\npub(crate) unsafe fn FSE_minTableLog_withClz(\n    srcSize: usize,\n    clzMaxSymbolValue: c_uint,\n) -> c_uint {\n    let minBitsSrc: U32 = ZSTD_highbit32(srcSize as U32).wrapping_add(1);\n    /* BIT_highbit32(mSV) + 2  ==  (31 - clz(mSV)) + 2  ==  33 - clz(mSV) */\n    let minBitsSymbols: U32 = 33u32.wrapping_sub(clzMaxSymbolValue);\n    let minBits: U32 = if minBitsSrc < minBitsSymbols {\n        minBitsSrc\n    } else {\n        minBitsSymbols\n    };\n    minBits\n}\n\n/// `FSE_minTableLog()`. For `maxSymbolValue == 0` the reference build's\n/// `ZSTD_highbit32()` returns 0 (see above), i.e. `clz` observably reads 31.\npub(crate) unsafe fn FSE_minTableLog(srcSize: usize, maxSymbolValue: c_uint) -> c_uint {\n    let clz = if maxSymbolValue == 0 {\n        31\n    } else {\n        ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32(maxSymbolValue)\n    };\n    FSE_minTableLog_withClz(srcSize, clz)\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1426,"cache_read_input_tokens":179518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1426,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Vw3T2VXPmk7ueJw4J26uBW","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a","uuid":"e4e3d0c5-0326-433d-bcbb-c8c6e33087a6","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:30:44.845Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write entropy differential tests"}
