{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xk4hdfk7ez2jkkmvw6jyk6kok2lvjia7caj5ysmh3jana7dngwvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files are complete and passing. No changes were needed to `translation/src/` — the Rust port matched the C ground truth on every case.\n\n## `tests/phase_b_zbuff.rs` (7 tests)\n`cfg_zbuff_compress`, `cfg_zbuff_compress_advanced`, `cfg_zbuff_dict`, `cfg_zbuff_decompress`, `cfg_zbuff_helpers`, `err_zbuff_params`, `err_zbuff_forwarding`\n\n```\ntest result: ok. 7 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.32s\n```\n\nEvery call records `{return value, *dstCapacityPtr, *srcSizePtr}` into a `Rec` sequence that is compared between libs, plus the full output byte stream, plus a `ZSTD_decompress` / `ZSTD_decompress_usingDict` re-decode in *both* libs checked against the original input. Covers CONFIGS 170–175 and ERRORS 272, 274–277. `ZSTD_getParams` results are cross-checked before being fed to `ZBUFF_compressInit_advanced`.\n\n## `tests/phase_b_legacy.rs` (9 tests)\n`legacy_v01` … `legacy_v07`, `legacy_entropy`, `legacy_isError`\n\n```\ntest result: ok. 9 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.10s\n```\n\nCorpus per version: correct magic alone (v01 big-endian `0xFD2FB51E`, v02–v07 little-endian `0xFD2FB522`–`527`, verified against the headers), wrong-endian spelling, magic + 64/256 B deterministic garbage, the 14 hand-built plausible-but-corrupt header tails, a modern `ZSTD_compress` frame (and its body behind the legacy magic), 0/1/2/3/4/5-byte buffers, 1024 all-zero bytes — **plus** an exhaustive 1-byte sweep of the frame-header-descriptor and 3-byte block-header positions (×random/zero payload), ~1070 buffers per version. Instrumented coverage: ~10,000 batteries, ~480 producing a *successful* legacy decompress, ~9,900 exercising `decompressContinue`.\n\nAll 283 referenced legacy/ZBUFF/FSE/HUF symbols are covered. Notable facts discovered from `nm`, handled via an optional-symbol helper that asserts C and Rust agree on *presence*:\n- `ZSTDv02_decompressDCtx` / `ZSTDv03_decompressDCtx` are declared in the headers but **not exported**.\n- `ZSTDv04_isError` / `ZSTDv04_getErrorName` are **not exported** (so `legacy_isError` sweeps v01,02,03,05,06,07).\n- `HUFv06_isError` / `HUFv06_getErrorName` are **not exported**.\n- `ZSTDv06_compressBound` is declared in `zstd_v06.h` but **not exported** (no legacy encoder).\n\nStruct/size checks that agreed exactly: `ZSTDv05_sizeofDCtx`, `ZSTDv06_sizeofDCtx`, `ZSTDv07_sizeofDCtx`, `ZSTDv07_estimateDCtxSize`, and the full `ZSTDv05_parameters` / `ZSTDv06_frameParams` / `ZSTDv07_frameParams` out-structs. `findFrameSizeInfoLegacy` compares both `cSize` and `dBound`. C objects are only ever passed to C functions and Rust objects to Rust functions (including `copyDCtx` / `decompress_usingPreparedDCtx` pairs and `createDDict`/`freeDDict`).\n\n## Divergences\nNone. Two initial failures were bugs in my own test expectations, not the port:\n1. I had asserted the C `isError` matches the harness's `is_error()` helper — they differ at exactly `(size_t)-120` (real `ERR_isError` is `code > (size_t)-120`, strict; the harness helper uses `<= 120`). Both libraries agreed with each other; I dropped that cross-check.\n2. My \"must be rejected\" cParams list wrongly included in-bounds values (e.g. `searchLog=1`); replaced with per-parameter bounds tables derived from `zstd.h` (`WINDOWLOG 10..31`, `CHAINLOG`/`HASHLOG 6..30`, `SEARCHLOG 1..30`, `MINMATCH 3..7`, `STRATEGY 1..9`).\n\nA deliberate fault-injection run was used to confirm the record-comparison harness actually fails on divergence (it did, for all 7 version tests).\n\nOnly `tests/phase_b_zbuff.rs` and `tests/phase_b_legacy.rs` were created; nothing else was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1165,"cache_read_input_tokens":204442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1165,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WfBCFTShmHPteAvSM4LnN5","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a","uuid":"4ee120df-badc-4d78-ae47-63918787e71d","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:31:35.299Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write ZBUFF and legacy tests"}
