os32(0) == 31` and **`ZSTD_highbit32(0) == 0`**. The Rust version computed `31 - 32`, wrapping to `0xFFFFFFFF`. Verified by disassembling `ZSTD_countLeadingZeros32`/`ZSTD_highbit32`/`FSE_minTableLog`/`FSE_optimalTableLog_internal` at `0x11c94`/`0x11ca4`/`0x12c5a`/`0x12c9d`.\n\n1. **`translation/src/bits.rs` — `ZSTD_highbit32()`**: now returns `0` for `val == 0` (documented with the `bsr` rationale). Fixes e.g. `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal(9,1,1,0)`: C `5`, Rust was `9`.\n2. **`translation/src/compress/fse_compress.rs` — `FSE_minTableLog()`**: now passes `clz == 31` when `maxSymbolValue == 0`.\n3. **`translation/src/compress/fse_compress.rs` — `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal()` and `FSE_normalizeCount()`**: removed two stale bespoke UB emulations (`clz(srcSize-1)` and `31 ^ (U32)total`) that were derived from an *inlined* build and are wrong for this reference build; both now just call `FSE_minTableLog()`. Fixes e.g. `FSE_optimalTableLog_internal(9,4096,0,0)` (C `9`, Rust was `12`) and `FSE_normalizeCount(tableLog=9,total=4096,maxSymbolValue=0)` (C returned `9` with a filled `normalizedCounter`, Rust returned `-1`/GENERIC).\n\n## Upstream quirk worth knowing (test-side workaround, no source change)\n\n`FSE_BUILD_CTABLE_WORKSPACE_SIZE_U32(maxSymbolValue, tableLog)` under-counts by 2 bytes whenever `maxSymbolValue + 2 + tableSize` is odd (integer-division truncation), while `FSE_buildCTable_wksp()` lays down a `spread` table of `tableSize + 8` bytes after `tableSymbol`. Both C and Rust therefore write 2 bytes past a macro-sized workspace (reproduced with canary padding, e.g. `tableLog=5, maxSymbolValue=1`; it also applies to `maxSymbolValue=255`). The test allocates 16 extra `u32` of slack but still passes the *macro-computed* `wkspSize` so the internal size check behaves identically — and it compares the slack region as well, which C and Rust fill identically.","usage":{"total_tokens":235407,"tool_uses":86,"duration_ms":1749437},"uuid":"19b28be2-9110-45d0-b6a6-55d049278a5d","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a"}
