ut byte across all configurations. All the initial failures were bugs in my test harness, not in the port.\n\n## Conditions that turned out to be unreachable / UB (documented in comments, not faked)\n- **ERRORS 259** (`ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min` narrowing overflow): impossible on a 64-bit target where `size_t == unsigned long long`. Both libs are still compared over a large window/FCS matrix incl. `u64::MAX` wrap-around cases.\n- **ERRORS 138** (`compressSequencesAndLiterals` empty frame, `dstCapacity < 3`): `ZSTD_writeFrameHeader` runs first and requires `dstCapacity >= ZSTD_FRAMEHEADERSIZE_MAX` (18), so ≥3 bytes always remain. Also, the empty-frame sequence array itself fails earlier with `externalSequences_invalid` (107) because `decompressedSize == 0` ⇒ `maxNbSeq == 0`.\n- **ERRORS 120** (`generateSequences`, `nbWorkers != 0`) and **89/90** (`estimate*_usingCCtxParams`, `nbWorkers > 0`): this is a non-MT build, so `setParameter(nbWorkers>0)` is itself rejected; verified both libs reject identically and that the estimates still match.\n- **ERRORS 30** (`createCCtxParams` customMem XOR): `ZSTD_createCCtxParams_advanced` is `static` and not exported; only the always-default path is reachable.\n- **ERRORS 187** partial: `ZSTD_frameHeaderSize(NULL, n>0)` dereferences unconditionally, so only `ZSTD_getFrameHeader(_advanced)` is called with NULL.\n- `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams(NULL)` dereferences unconditionally — not exercised (was my initial SIGSEGV).\n- `ZSTD_compressSuperBlock` cannot be driven standalone (consumes an already-built seqStore + block-state entropy tables); exercised through `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize` compression with byte-exact frame comparison and round-trip.\n- `ZSTD_get1BlockSummary` on a delimiter-less array sets only `nbSequences` (to an error code) and leaves `blockSize`/`litSize` **uninitialized** in C — so only `nbSequences` is compared in that case. This was a real trap: comparing the whole struct produced spurious failures from C stack garbage.\n- `ZSTD_freeThreadPool` / `ZSTD_createThreadPool` are not exported by this build.\n\n## Notable API facts discovered while iterating\n- `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` returns the *sanitized value*, not 0.\n- `ZSTD_compressStream2(..., ZSTD_e_end)` as the first call turns the available input size into `pledgedSrcSize`, so it emits an FCS field. Producing a genuinely unknown-FCS frame requires an initial `ZSTD_e_continue` call.\n- `ZSTD_DCtx_setParameter(ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts, …)` on a static DCtx fails for *any* value including 0 (the static check sits after the bounds check, before the assignment).\n- `MIN_DST_CAP = 18` is mandatory for `ZSTD_compressSequences` / `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals`; smaller capacities underflow the remaining-capacity arithmetic under NDEBUG.\n\n`cfg_seqstore_internals` drives the internals for real: `ZSTD_getSeqStore` (full field-by-field + SeqDef array + literals comparison), `ZSTD_seqToCodes` (ll/ml/of code arrays), `ZSTD_crossEntropyCost`, `ZSTD_buildCTable` for all four encoding types (comparing NCount bytes, the built FSE_CTable, and the in-place-modified count array), `ZSTD_fseBitCost`, `ZSTD_selectEncodingType` over all repeatMode × policy × strategy combinations, `ZSTD_encodeSequences` with freshly built set_compressed tables (bmi2 0/1), `ZSTD_buildBlockEntropyStats` (metadata + nextEntropy buffers compared byte-for-byte), and `ZSTD_resetSeqStore`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":605,"cache_read_input_tokens":312473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":605,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JDS6Ufv671L4hjddpjV1bD","session_id":"2a31ca95-dd24-43a5-a333-deba8c9ab59a","uuid":"ab4f34ce-5b52-4137-b1a7-7d1898ef080b","timestamp":"2026-09-08T18:43:54.641Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write framein